WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
When I first learned Git, one of the most
confusing topics to me was merge

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.069
conflicts. It seems like I always found
myself in a merge conflict I didn't know

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:11.099
why and I didn't know how to get out of
it. But really they're not that

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:15.900
complicated. A merge conflict occurs when
there's been a change in the same file

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:21.090
in the same line on the two branches
you're trying to merge together. So here,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.920
for example, if we're working in index.html on two branches and there have been

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.890
changes in line four in both files that will
generate a merge conflict. Now, for

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.270
example ,this is just one conflict there
could be multiple files or even multiple

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.670
portions of the same file with conflicts
but for now let's keep it simple. So, Git

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.050
tells you there's a conflict.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:47.579
What do you do next? My favorite next
step is to run 'git status'.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:51.660
It's an easy way to clear my head and
see exactly which files have the

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:56.070
conflicts in them. Once I know what file
to look at, I open it up in my favorite

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.079
text editor and I look for these merge
conflict markers. Once you find the merge

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:05.250
conflict markers, all you need to do is
pick the version of code that you'd like

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:10.200
to keep and get rid of the merge
conflict markers. One version will be

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.580
above equal signs and the other will be
below. You can pick one, delete them both,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.619
or create something totally new.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:20.909
Git doesn't care. Just make sure the code
looks the way you want it to and get rid

00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.470
of the merge conflict markers. Save those
changes and commit them and Git will

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.270
know the merge conflict has resolved.

